aak-marketing — additional third-party sources
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Many skills, agents, and workflows in `plugins/aak-marketing/` are adapted from
the following upstream projects. Each is credited here; their license terms
apply to the adapted portions.

- antigravity-marketing (https://github.com/nguyenphp/antigravity-marketing),
  Copyright (c) NguyenPHP, MIT (as declared in the project's package.json and
  README). Source of most marketing skills, the 4 marketing agents, and the
  /campaign, /content, /optimize, /analyze, /report, /brand-report workflows.
  Includes the `vision-analysis` skill, re-pointed from the paid MiniMax vision
  tool to Claude's native image reading (MiniMax kept as an optional fallback).
  Deliberate mechanical deviations from the upstream (frontmatter/wiring only,
  bodies unchanged): (a) stale "Related Skills" cross-refs that dangle in the
  upstream itself were re-pointed to this kit's real skill names
  (`ab-test-setup`→`ab-test-dashboard`, `seo-audit`→`seo-fundamentals`,
  `analytics-tracking`→`analytics-marketing`), and a self-referential ref in
  `signup-flow-cro` was corrected to `form-cro` (both upstreams already say
  `form-cro`); (b) three skills whose upstream frontmatter `name:` did not match
  their directory (`competitor-teardown`→was `competitor-teardown-agent`,
  `competitor-monitor`→was `competitor-monitor-alert`,
  `content-repurposing`→was `content-repurposing-pipeline`; the suffixes matched
  no upstream agent and nothing references them) were normalized to `name = dir`.

- ClaudeKit (https://claudekit.cc / https://github.com/mrgoonie/claudekit-skills),
  by claudekit. Source of the `brand` and `banner-design` skills. Both were
  adapted to run standalone (the `brand` token-sync script was made
  self-contained; `banner-design` image/screenshot steps were repointed to
  available image-generation and browser tools).

- MiniMax-AI/skills (https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/skills), Copyright (c) 2026
  MiniMax, MIT. Source of the `minimax-pdf` skill (styled, local PDF generation).

- Remotion Dev Skills (https://github.com/remotion-dev/skills), by Remotion.
  Source of `remotion-best-practices`, `video-automation`, `tutorial-video-expert`.

- vibeship-spawner-skills, Apache License 2.0. Source of the
  `viral-generator-builder` skill. Under Apache-2.0, this notice preserves the
  attribution; see the upstream project for the full license text.

- Antigravity Awesome Skills (https://github.com/sickn33/antigravity-awesome-skills),
  community-contributed. Origin of several patterns (e.g. `marketing-ideas`,
  the CRO-suite skills, `programmatic-seo`) as bundled via antigravity-marketing.

- ai-marketing-claude (https://github.com/zubair-trabzada/ai-marketing-claude),
  Copyright (c) 2026 Zubair Trabzada, MIT. Source of: the `client-proposal` skill
  and its proposal template; the email/content/launch templates bundled under
  `email-marketing`, `content-marketing`, and `launch-strategy`; the verbatim
  scoring rubrics, weights, and report format in the `site-audit` skill (its five
  audit-dimension rubric files are copied from that project's audit subagents); and
  `site-audit/scripts/analyze_page.py` (parsing/scoring logic unchanged; a
  network-safety wrapper was added in front of the fetchers). The `/audit` command
  wires these to this kit's own marketing agents rather than vendoring theirs.

- agentkits-marketing (https://github.com/aitytech/agentkits-marketing),
  Copyright (c) AityTech, MIT. Source of the net-new marketing skills `schema-markup`,
  `form-cro`, `free-tool-strategy`, `copy-editing`, and `email-sequence` (SKILL.md
  bodies and their `references/` guides vendored verbatim). Only mechanical wiring
  changed: frontmatter reduced to this kit's `name`/`description` convention (their
  `triggers` folded into the description; `brand`/`agents`/`related_skills`/
  `mcp_integrations`/`success_metrics` dropped), and a few "Related Skills" prose
  refs re-pointed to this kit's skill names (`ab-test-setup`→`ab-test-dashboard`,
  `seo-audit`→`seo-fundamentals`, `analytics-tracking`→`analytics-marketing`), and
  a "Reference guide" pointer line was appended to each SKILL.md so the bundled
  `references/` guide is discoverably loaded. Vendored from upstream commit
  e1d08b66899795bfaddbb42a1843b1bcb9e0f688 (2026-07-15).
  This project shares a common ancestor with
  antigravity-marketing / ai-marketing-claude above.

- vietnamese-language-skill (https://github.com/trussary/vietnamese-language-skill),
  Copyright (c) trussary, MIT. Vendored verbatim as the `aak-vietnamese` plugin —
  the five `vietnamese-*` skills (SKILL.md bodies, references, and the dependency-free
  `validate_copy.py` linter + domain `rules_*.py`), the shared references, and the eval
  corpus, byte-identical to pinned commit
  1c44546d7862e0d09491a2a711a64086ab8c80d7 (2026-08-22) except for the two
  mechanical wiring changes noted here. Changed: `plugin.json` identity fields
  (name/author/homepage/repository); and the reference-doc `CONTRIBUTING.md`
  links in the `examples.md`/`register-guide.md` files were re-pointed from the
  upstream repo-root path to this kit's own `CONTRIBUTING.md`
  (https://github.com/HDShinobi/ai-agentic-kit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md), since
  contributions are accepted through this repository. Added: a non-vendored
  acceptance harness (`.acceptance/replay_evals.py`).

Where an upstream skill shipped a placeholder/stub library (marketing-ideas,
marketing-psychology), the missing content was authored fresh for this project.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
aak-ads — additional third-party source
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `plugins/aak-ads/` plugin is vendored from Claude Ads
(https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-ads), Copyright (c) 2026 agricidaniel,
MIT. It is copied verbatim: the `ads/` skill router and its 38 references, the
33 `ads-*` workflow skills (with `ads-plan/assets/`), the 25 audit/creative/
release agents, the `claude_ads_core/` deterministic scoring engine and v1
schemas, the `control-plane/` manifests and schemas, the `scripts/` helpers,
the `evals/`, and the `tests/` (with fixtures) — substance byte-identical to
upstream. The plugin's own `LICENSE` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` (which
enumerates its runtime dependency licenses) are retained under
`plugins/aak-ads/`.

Only mechanical wiring changed: `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` identity fields
(name → `aak-ads`, author, homepage) were rewritten for this kit; the upstream
repo-governance and host files (README, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING, install/
uninstall scripts and their receipt/verify helpers, `.github/`, per-host
CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/GEMINI.md/CODEX.md, the upstream marketplace.json, and
`assets/`) were dropped as they do not apply inside this marketplace. Two
repo-governance tests coupled to those dropped/renamed identity files were
removed with them: `tests/scripts/test_installer_security.py` (tested the
dropped installer) and the single test case
`test_claude_command_contract_distinguishes_plugin_namespace` in
`tests/release/test_release.py` (asserted the dropped repo `README.md` exists
and documents the upstream `/claude-ads:ads` namespace, now `/aak-ads:ads`); the
other 49 cases in that file, which exercise the release/SBOM/inventory gate used
by `ads-validate`, are retained verbatim. No skill, agent, reference, rubric,
scoring, schema, or other product substance was paraphrased or re-derived.
